language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Flip the signs of whole rows and columns of the input matrix so that every row and every column sums to a non-negative number, minimising the overall sum.
given input_matrix_dim1, input_matrix_dim2 : int
given input_matrix : matrix indexed by [int(1..input_matrix_dim1), int(1..input_matrix_dim2)] of int
find row_signs : matrix indexed by [int(1..input_matrix_dim1)] of int(-1,1)
find col_signs : matrix indexed by [int(1..input_matrix_dim2)] of int(-1,1)
find total : int(-100000000..100000000)

branching on [col_signs, row_signs]

minimising total
such that
$ each row of the flipped matrix must sum to a positive number or zero
forAll i : int(1..input_matrix_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..input_matrix_dim2) . row_signs[i] * col_signs[j] * input_matrix[i,j]) >= 0,
$ each column of the flipped matrix must sum to a positive number or zero
forAll j : int(1..input_matrix_dim2) . (sum i : int(1..input_matrix_dim1) . row_signs[i] * col_signs[j] * input_matrix[i,j]) >= 0,
$ the overall sum is the sum of all entries of the flipped matrix
total = (sum i : int(1..input_matrix_dim1) . (sum j : int(1..input_matrix_dim2) . row_signs[i] * col_signs[j] * input_matrix[i,j]))
